A||||7||2M4 Dale||84 Fiero Sail Panels||||1||
Z||000000||2M4 Dale||09-27-2000||09:43 AM||||Help... How do I remove them with out destroying them ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-27-2000||10:06 AM||||Two clips and a 10mm stamped nut holds the sail panel on from the backside.<P>They're kind of a pain to remove but I take out the black filler panels on the inboard side to get access to the clips.  You can just reef on the panel and the clip will eventually let the studs go, but you risk breaking the window, ruining the rubber edge of the sail, the stud, or the rear clip.  <P>With the inside filler panel removed, you'll be able to see the clips.  Bend the tab on the lower clip and you'll easily release the stud on the sail.  You will need to remove the interior quarter panel piece to remove a stamped nut through a hole from the inside of the car.  Be careful not to drop the nut down inside, put some tape or sticky stuff on the inside of the socket to help the nut from falling off.<P>The second clip is about 4 or 5 inches from the top.  I believe that stud is thru a slot and by just pushing or pulling the sail panel forward the clip will slid out of the slot in the body.<P>Bend the tabs back so they will hold the studs again, put them back on the car and do the rest of the steps in reverse.<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">              <BR>              <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>   <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||09-27-2000||10:47 AM||||Big Hug for HugGRRRFiero...Thanks||||reg||14
